  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors\n",
        "author: \"CDS DS-121<br>Boston University\"\n",
        "format: \n",
        "    revealjs:\n",
        "        math: true\n",
        "        css: \n",
        "        - styles.css\n",
        "        html-math-method: mathjax\n",
        "        highlight-style: github\n",
        "        slide-number: true\n",
        "        show-slide-number: all\n",
        "        chalkboard: true\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Learning Objectives\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "- Definition of an eigenvector and an eigenvalue\n",
        "- Geometric interpretation of eigenvectors and eigenvalues\n",
        "- Definition of an eigenspace\n",
        "- Geometric interpretation of eigenspaces\n",
        "- Computation of eigenvalues and eigenvectors\n",
        "    - Characteristic polynomial\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Markov Chains\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}"
      ],
      "id": "def4b45c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from IPython.core.display import HTML\n",
        "\n",
        "def generate_html():\n",
        "    return r\"\"\"\n",
        "    <div class=\"blue-box\">\n",
        "        <p>\n",
        "Consider the Markov chain described by \\(P = \\begin{bmatrix}\n",
        "    0.7 & 0.6\\\\ 0.3 & 0.4\n",
        "\\end{bmatrix}\\) and initial probability vector \\(\\mathbf{x}_0 = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}.\\) Find the probability vector \\(\\mathbf{x}_2\\) specifying the probabilities of the states after 2 time periods.\n",
        "     <br>\n",
        "     <br>\n",
        "          <br>\n",
        "     <br>\n",
        "          <br>\n",
        "     <br>\n",
        "          <br>\n",
        "     <br>\n",
        "        </p>\n",
        "    </div>\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "html_content = generate_html()\n",
        "display(HTML(html_content))"
      ],
      "id": "7804ccd1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        ":::{.notes}\n",
        "    The question is asking us to compute $\\mathbf{x}_2$: \n",
        "\n",
        "    $$\\mathbf{x}_2 = P^2 \\mathbf{x}_0 = P(P\\mathbf{x}_0) = \\begin{bmatrix}\n",
        "    0.7 & 0.6\\\\ 0.3 & 0.4\n",
        "    \\end{bmatrix} \n",
        "    \\left(\n",
        "    \\begin{bmatrix}\n",
        "    0.7 & 0.6\\\\ 0.3 & 0.4\n",
        "    \\end{bmatrix} \n",
        "    \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \n",
        "    \\end{bmatrix} \n",
        "    \\right)= \n",
        "    \\begin{bmatrix}\n",
        "    0.7 & 0.6\\\\ 0.3 & 0.4\n",
        "    \\end{bmatrix} \n",
        "    \\begin{bmatrix} 0.6 \\\\ 0.4 \\end{bmatrix}\n",
        "    = \\begin{bmatrix} 0.66 \\\\ 0.34 \\end{bmatrix}.$$\n",
        "    \n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## The Value of Eigenvalues\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "* Better understanding of Markov Chains;\n",
        "\n",
        "* Concepts required for the PageRank algorithm and principle component analysis (PCA).\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.center-text}\n",
        "<img src=\"images/eigenvectors/boat.png\" width=700/>\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Eigenvectors\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "To explain eigenvalues, we first explain eigenvectors. \n",
        "\n",
        "Almost all vectors change direction, when they are multiplied by a matrix $A$. Certain exceptional vectors $\\mathbf{x}$ are in the same direction as $A \\mathbf{x}$. \n",
        "\n",
        "Those are the **eigenvectors.** Multiply an eigenvector $\\mathbf{x}$ by $A,$ and the vector $A \\mathbf{x}$ is a number $\\lambda$ times $\\mathbf{x}.$\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- :::{.center-text style=\"font-size: 1em\"} -->\n",
        "Consider $A = \\begin{bmatrix}3&-2\\\\1&0\\end{bmatrix}, \\mathbf{u} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}, \\mathbf{v}=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n",
        "<!-- ::: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- The images of $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ under multiplication by $A$ are shown geometrically here. -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- <br> -->"
      ],
      "id": "77b72037"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from IPython.core.display import HTML\n",
        "\n",
        "def generate_html():\n",
        "    return r\"\"\"\n",
        "    <div class=\"blue-box\">\n",
        "        <p>\n",
        "        Are \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) in the same direction as \\(A \\mathbf{u}\\) and \\(A \\mathbf{v}\\), respectively?\n",
        "        </p>\n",
        "    </div>\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "html_content = generate_html()\n",
        "display(HTML(html_content))"
      ],
      "id": "d339fa60",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Eigenvectors\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.center-text}"
      ],
      "id": "f2b43c3b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import laUtilities as ut\n",
        "\n",
        "#\n",
        "ax = ut.plotSetup(size=(10,6))\n",
        "ut.centerAxes(ax)\n",
        "A = np.array([[3,-2],[1,0]])\n",
        "u = np.array([-1,1])\n",
        "v = np.array([2,1])\n",
        "#\n",
        "ut.plotArrowVec(ax, v, [0,0], color='Red')\n",
        "ut.plotArrowVec(ax, A.dot(v), [0,0], color='Red')\n",
        "ax.text(v[0],v[1]+0.2,r'${\\bf v}$',size=20)\n",
        "ax.text(A.dot(v)[0],A.dot(v)[1]+0.2,r'$A{\\bf v}$',size=20)\n",
        "#\n",
        "ut.plotArrowVec(ax, u, [0,0], color='Blue')\n",
        "ut.plotArrowVec(ax, A.dot(u), [0,0], color='Blue')\n",
        "ax.text(u[0]-0.5,u[1]+0.1,r'${\\bf u}$',size=20)\n",
        "ax.text(A.dot(u)[0]-0.7,A.dot(u)[1]+0.3,r'$A{\\bf u}$',size=20);"
      ],
      "id": "4f5d39cc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}"
      ],
      "id": "57060991"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from IPython.core.display import HTML\n",
        "\n",
        "def generate_html():\n",
        "    return r\"\"\"\n",
        "    <div class=\"purple-box\">\n",
        "        <p><span class=\"label\">Eigenvector and eigenvalue</span>\n",
        "        An <b>eigenvector</b> of an \\(n\\times n\\) matrix \\(A\\) is a nonzero vector \\(\\mathbf{x}\\) such that \\(A\\mathbf{x} = \\lambda\\mathbf{x}\\) for some scalar \\(\\lambda.\\) The scalar \\(\\lambda\\) is an <b>eigenvalue</b> of \\(A\\).\n",
        "    \n",
        "        </p>\n",
        "    </div>\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "html_content = generate_html()\n",
        "display(HTML(html_content))"
      ],
      "id": "009e1963",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "<br>"
      ],
      "id": "cf5a6376"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from IPython.core.display import HTML\n",
        "\n",
        "def generate_html():\n",
        "    return r\"\"\"\n",
        "    <div class=\"purple-box\">\n",
        "        <p><span class=\"label\">Eigenspace</span>\n",
        "        The set of all eigenvectors corresponding to a particular eigenvalue \\(\\lambda\\) is called the <b>eigenspace of \\(A\\) corresponding to \\(\\lambda\\)</b>.\n",
        "        </p>\n",
        "    </div>\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "html_content = generate_html()\n",
        "display(HTML(html_content))"
      ],
      "id": "b3daf362",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "The eigenvalue $\\lambda$ tells whether the eigenvector $\\mathbf{x}$ is streched or shrunk or reversed or left unchanged, when it is multiplied by $A.$\n",
        "\n",
        "We may find $\\lambda = 2$ or $\\frac{1}{2}$ or $-1$ or $1$. _**The eigenvalue $\\lambda$ could be zero!**_\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "__Example.__  Let $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1&6\\\\5&2\\end{bmatrix}, \\mathbf{u} = \\begin{bmatrix}6\\\\-5\\end{bmatrix}, \\mathbf{v}=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\\\-2\\end{bmatrix}.$  \n",
        "\n",
        "Are $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ eigenvectors of $A$?\n",
        "\n",
        "__Solution.__\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{bmatrix}1&6\\\\5&2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6\\\\-5\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-24\\\\20\\end{bmatrix} = -4\\begin{bmatrix}6\\\\-5\\end{bmatrix} = -4\\mathbf{u}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{bmatrix}1&6\\\\5&2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3\\\\-2\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-9\\\\11\\end{bmatrix} \\neq \\lambda\\begin{bmatrix}3\\\\-2\\end{bmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "So $\\mathbf{u}$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $-4$, but $\\mathbf{v}$ is not an eigenvector of $A$.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}"
      ],
      "id": "2dcaaa80"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from IPython.core.display import HTML\n",
        "\n",
        "def generate_html():\n",
        "    return r\"\"\"\n",
        "    <div class=\"blue-box\">\n",
        "        <p>\n",
        "        Let \\(A= \\begin{bmatrix}0.8&0.3\\\\ 0.2&0.7 \\end{bmatrix}\\). Are \\(\\mathbf{x}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}0.6\\\\ 0.4 \\end{bmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{x}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}1\\\\ -1 \\end{bmatrix}\\) eigenvectors of \\(A?\\) If so, what are the corresponding eigenvalues?<br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br>\n",
        "        </p>\n",
        "    </div>\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "html_content = generate_html()\n",
        "display(HTML(html_content))"
      ],
      "id": "20da42c0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "__Example.__   Show that 7 is an eigenvalue of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1&6\\\\5&2\\end{bmatrix}$, and find the corresponding eigenvectors.\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- <br> -->\n",
        "\n",
        "__Solution.__ For 7 to be an eigenvalue of $A$, it must be the case that \n",
        "\n",
        "$$ \n",
        "A\\mathbf{x}=7\\mathbf{x}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "has a nontrivial solution.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is equivalent to:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$ \n",
        "A\\mathbf{x} - 7\\mathbf{x} = {\\bf 0}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A\\mathbf{x} - 7I\\mathbf{x} = {\\bf 0}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "(A - 7I)\\mathbf{x} = {\\bf 0}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "<!-- To solve this homogeneous equation, form the matrix -->\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A - 7I = \\begin{bmatrix}1&6\\\\5&2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}7&0\\\\0&7\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-6&6\\\\5&-5\\end{bmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$A-7I$ is a square matrix whose columns are linearly dependent, so by the IMT $(A - 7I)\\mathbf{x} = {\\bf 0}$ has a nontrivial solution. Hence, 7 is an eigenvalue of $A$.\n",
        "\n",
        "To find the corresponding eigenvectors, we solve $(A - 7I)\\mathbf{x} = {\\bf 0}$ using row operations:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-6&6&0\\\\5&-5&0\\end{array}\\right]\n",
        "\\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1&-1&0\\\\0&0&0\\end{array}\\right].\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This says that $x_1 = x_2,$ and $x_2$ is free. So the general solution is $x_2\\begin{bmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Each vector of this form with $x_2 \\neq 0$ is an eigenvector corresponding to $\\lambda = 7.$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenspace\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "From the previous example, we can conclude that $\\lambda$ _**is an eigenvalue of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A$ if and only if the equation**_\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "(A-\\lambda I)\\mathbf{x} = {\\bf 0}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "_**has a nontrivial solution.**_\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "As a result, the _**eigenspace**_ (i.e., the set of all eigenvectors) of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda$ is just _**the null space of the matrix**_ $A-\\lambda I.$ That is, the eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda$ make up the null space of $A-\\lambda I.$\n",
        "\n",
        "Hence, the eigenspace is a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^n.$ \n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ```{python}\n",
        "from IPython.core.display import HTML\n",
        "\n",
        "def generate_html():\n",
        "    return r\"\"\"\n",
        "    <div class=\"blue-box\">\n",
        "        <p>\n",
        "        How many eigenvectors can an \\(n \\times n\\) matrix have? \n",
        "        </p>\n",
        "    </div>\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "html_content = generate_html()\n",
        "display(HTML(html_content))\n",
        "``` -->\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ## Finding the Eigenspace\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "Recall that the dimension of a null space can be anywhere from $0$ to $n$, where $n$ is the number of columns.\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "If the dimension of an eigenspace is 0, then $\\lambda$ is not an eigenvalue of $A$. If the dimension of an eigenspace is $n$, there are $n$ linearly independent eigenvectors of $A$.\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "If $A$ is the identity matrix in $\\mathbb{R}^{2 \\times 2}$, all vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ are its eigenvectors. The only eigenvalue of $I$ is 1. This is unusual. Most $2 \\times 2$ matrices have 2 eigenvector directions and 2 eigenvalues.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenspace\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "For matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1&6\\\\5&2\\end{bmatrix}$, we found that the general solution for the eigenvector corresponding to $\\lambda = 7$ is the expression $x_2\\begin{bmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}.$  \n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "This means that the eigenspace of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda = 7$ consists of all multiples of $\\begin{bmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{bmatrix},$ which is the line through $(1,1)$ and the origin but excluding the origin (recall the zero vector cannot be an eigenvector).\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "We could also show that the eigenspace corresponding to $\\lambda = -4$ is the line through $(-6, 5)$, again excluding the origin.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenspace\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        ":::{.center-text}"
      ],
      "id": "c8ff819a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#\n",
        "ax = ut.plotSetup(-10,10,-6,10,size=(10,7))\n",
        "ut.centerAxes(ax)\n",
        "A = np.array([[1,6],[5,2]])\n",
        "u = np.array([1,1])\n",
        "v = np.array([3./2,-5./4])\n",
        "#\n",
        "ax.plot(v[0],v[1],'bo')\n",
        "ax.plot(A.dot(v)[0],A.dot(v)[1],'bo')\n",
        "ax.text(v[0],v[1]+0.2,r'${\\bf v}$',size=20)\n",
        "ax.text(A.dot(v)[0]+0.2,A.dot(v)[1]+0.2,r'$A{\\bf v}$',size=20)\n",
        "ax.plot([-10,10],[5*10/6.0,-5*10/6.0],'b-',lw=2)\n",
        "#\n",
        "ax.plot(u[0],u[1],'ro')\n",
        "ax.plot(A.dot(u)[0],A.dot(u)[1],'ro')\n",
        "ax.text(u[0]+0.7,u[1],r'${\\bf u}$',size=20)\n",
        "ax.text(A.dot(u)[0]+0.7,A.dot(u)[1],r'$A{\\bf u}$',size=20)\n",
        "ax.plot([-6,10],[-6,10],'r-',lw=2)\n",
        "# \n",
        "ax.annotate('', xy=(A.dot(u)[0], A.dot(u)[1]),  xycoords='data',\n",
        "                xytext=(u[0], u[1]), textcoords='data',\n",
        "                size=18,\n",
        "                #bbox=dict(boxstyle=\"round\", fc=\"0.8\"),\n",
        "                arrowprops={'arrowstyle': 'simple',\n",
        "                                'fc': '0.5', \n",
        "                                'ec': 'none',\n",
        "                                'connectionstyle' : 'arc3,rad=0.5'},\n",
        "                )\n",
        "ax.annotate('', xy=(A.dot(v)[0], A.dot(v)[1]),  xycoords='data',\n",
        "                xytext=(v[0], v[1]), textcoords='data',\n",
        "                size=18,\n",
        "                #bbox=dict(boxstyle=\"round\", fc=\"0.8\"),\n",
        "                arrowprops={'arrowstyle': 'simple',\n",
        "                                'fc': '0.5', \n",
        "                                'ec': 'none',\n",
        "                                'connectionstyle' : 'arc3,rad=-0.5'},\n",
        "                )\n",
        "ax.text(3,9,r'Eigenspace for $\\lambda$ = 7',size=16)\n",
        "ax.text(-9.5,8,r'Eigenspace for $\\lambda = -4$',size=16);"
      ],
      "id": "e1243aca",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenspace\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "We can also find the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1&6\\\\5&2\\end{bmatrix}$ using `numpy`.\n",
        ":::"
      ],
      "id": "5c774509"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "A = np.array([[1, 6],\n",
        "              [5, 2]])\n",
        "\n",
        "# calculate eigenvalues and eigenvectors\n",
        "eigvals, eigvecs = np.linalg.eig(A)\n",
        "\n",
        "# print the results, rounded to 5 decimal places\n",
        "for i in range(len(eigvals)):\n",
        "    print(\"A has eigenvalue\", np.round(eigvals[i], 5), \"with eigenvector\", np.round(eigvecs[:,i], 5))"
      ],
      "id": "dd72edeb",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "In general, when we know the eigenvalue $\\lambda,$ we find the eigenvector by solving $(A-\\lambda I) \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{0}.$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenspace\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .75em\"}\n",
        "__Example.__  Let $A = \\begin{bmatrix}4&-1&6\\\\2&1&6\\\\2&-1&8\\end{bmatrix}.$  An eigenvalue of $A$ is $2.$  Find a basis for the the corresponding eigenspace.\n",
        "\n",
        "__Solution.__  The eigenspace we are looking for is the nullspace of\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .6em\"}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A - 2I = \\begin{bmatrix}4&-1&6\\\\2&1&6\\\\2&-1&8\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2&0&0\\\\0&2&0\\\\0&0&2\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}2&-1&6\\\\2&-1&6\\\\2&-1&6\\end{bmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .75em\"}\n",
        "Let's row reduce the augmented matrix for $(A-2I)\\mathbf{x}={\\bf 0}$:\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .6em\"}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2&-1&6&0\\\\2&-1&6&0\\\\2&-1&6&0\\end{array}\\right]\n",
        "\\sim\n",
        "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1&-1/2&3&0\\\\0&0&0&0\\\\0&0&0&0\\end{array}\\right]\n",
        "$$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .75em\"}\n",
        "2 is indeed an eigenvalue of $A,$ because $(A-2I)\\mathbf{x} = {\\bf 0}$ has a non-trivial solution.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenspace\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .75em\"}\n",
        "- All solutions lie on the plane $x_1 = \\frac{1}{2}x_2 -3x_3.$\n",
        "\n",
        "- Expressed as a vector, the general solution is: $\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}x_2 - 3x_3\\\\x_2\\\\x_3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n",
        "\n",
        "- Expressed as a vector sum, this is: $x_2\\begin{bmatrix}1/2\\\\1\\\\0\\end{bmatrix} + x_3\\begin{bmatrix}-3\\\\0\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}$ with $x_2$ and $x_3$ free.\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "So this eigenspace is a two-dimensional subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^3,$ and a basis for this subspace is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1/2\\\\1\\\\0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-3\\\\0\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenvalues\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "_**How do we find the eigenvalues?**_\n",
        "\n",
        "If $(A- \\lambda I)\\mathbf{x} = {\\bf 0}$ has a nonzero solution, $A - \\lambda I$ is not invertible. By the IMT, the determinant of $A - \\lambda I$ must be zero.\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>"
      ],
      "id": "2a2f9544"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from IPython.core.display import HTML\n",
        "\n",
        "def generate_html():\n",
        "    return r\"\"\"\n",
        "    <div class=\"purple-box\">\n",
        "        <p><span class=\"label\">Theorem</span>\n",
        "        The scalar \\(\\lambda\\) is an eigenvalue of \\(A\\) if and only if \\(A - \\lambda I\\) is singular (i.e., \\(\\operatorname{det}(A - \\lambda I) = 0\\)).\n",
        "        </p>\n",
        "    </div>\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "html_content = generate_html()\n",
        "display(HTML(html_content))"
      ],
      "id": "2541730a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "For any $n \\times n$ matrix, $\\operatorname{det}(A - \\lambda I)$ is a polynomial of degree $n,$ called the __characteristic polynomial__ of $A.$\n",
        "\n",
        "The equation $\\operatorname{det}(A - \\lambda I)$ is known as the __characteristic equation.__\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenvalues\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "__Example.__  Find the eigenvalues of $A = \\begin{bmatrix}2&3\\\\3&-6\\end{bmatrix}.$\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "__Solution.__  We must find all scalars $\\lambda$ such that the matrix equation\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "(A-\\lambda I)\\mathbf{x} = {\\bf 0}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "has a nontrivial solution. This problem is equivalent to finding all $\\lambda$ such that the matrix $A-\\lambda I$ is not invertible, or equivalently, $\\operatorname{det}(A - \\lambda I)=0.$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A - \\lambda I = \\begin{bmatrix}2&3\\\\3&-6\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}\\lambda&0\\\\0&\\lambda\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}2-\\lambda&3\\\\3&-6-\\lambda\\end{bmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenvalues\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "The eigenvalues of $A$ are the solutions of the characteristic equation\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{eqnarray*}\n",
        "0 &=& \\det(A-\\lambda I) \\\\\n",
        "&=& \\det\\begin{bmatrix}2-\\lambda&3\\\\3&-6-\\lambda\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n",
        "&=& (2-\\lambda)(-6-\\lambda)-(3)(3) \\\\\n",
        "&=& -12 + 6\\lambda -2\\lambda + \\lambda^2 - 9 \\\\\n",
        "&=& \\lambda^2+4\\lambda-21 \\\\\n",
        "&=& (\\lambda-3)(\\lambda + 7)\n",
        "\\end{eqnarray*}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "If $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0,$ then $\\lambda = 3$ or $\\lambda = -7.$  So the eigenvalues of $A$ are $3$ and $-7$.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenvalues\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "__Example.__  Find the characteristic equation of \n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .6em\"}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A = \\begin{bmatrix}5&-2&6&-1\\\\0&3&-8&0\\\\0&0&5&4\\\\0&0&0&1\\end{bmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "__Solution.__  Form $A - \\lambda I$ and note that $\\det (A)$ is the product of the entries on the diagonal of $A,$ if $A$ is triangular.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .6em\"}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\det(A-\\lambda I) = \\det\\begin{bmatrix}5-\\lambda&-2&6&-1\\\\0&3-\\lambda&-8&0\\\\0&0&5-\\lambda&4\\\\0&0&0&1-\\lambda\\end{bmatrix}\n",
        "=(5-\\lambda)(3-\\lambda)(5-\\lambda)(1-\\lambda).\n",
        "$$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .8em\"}\n",
        "So the characteristic equation is: \n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: .6em\"}\n",
        "$$(\\lambda-5)^2(\\lambda-3)(\\lambda-1) = \\lambda^4 - 14\\lambda^3 + 68 \\lambda^2 - 130\\lambda + 75 = 0.$$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors{.really-really-smaller-title}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: 1.35em\"}\n",
        "In summary, to find the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of an $n \\times n$ matrix $A,$ we follow these steps.\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "1. _Compute the determinant of $A - \\lambda I$_. With $\\lambda$ subtracted along the diagonal, this determinant starts with $\\lambda^n$ or $- \\lambda^n.$ It is a polynomial in $\\lambda$ of degree $n.$\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "2. _Find the roots of this polynomial_ by solving $\\operatorname{det}(A - \\lambda I)=0.$ The $n$ roots are the $n$ eigenvalues of $A.$ They make $A - \\lambda I$ singular.\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "3. For each eigenvalue $\\lambda,$ solve $(A - \\lambda I)\\mathbf{x}=0$ to _find an eigenvector $\\mathbf{x}.$_\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors{.really-really-smaller-title}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: 1.35em\"}\n",
        "__Example.__  Let $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\2&4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find its eigenvalues and eigenvectors.\n",
        "\n",
        "__Solution.__   1. Compute the determinant of $A - \\lambda I.$ \n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A - \\lambda I = \\begin{bmatrix}1- \\lambda &2\\\\2&4 - \\lambda \\end{bmatrix}.\n",
        "$$ \n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{det}(A - \\lambda I) = (1 - \\lambda)(4 - \\lambda) - (2)(2) = \\lambda^2 - 5 \\lambda.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Set this determinant to zero:\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.center-text}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\lambda^2 - 5 \\lambda = \\lambda(\\lambda - 5) = 0.\n",
        "$$ \n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "Hence, the eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\lambda_1=0$ and $\\lambda_2=5.$\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors{.really-really-smaller-title}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: 1.3em\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "3. It remains to find the eigenvectors. Solve $\\operatorname{det}(A - \\lambda I) = 0$ seperately for $\\lambda_1 = 0$ and $\\lambda_2=5.$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\left[ A - 0I \\,\\middle|\\, \\mathbf{0} \\right] = \n",
        "\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc|c}\n",
        "1 & 2 & 0 \\\\\n",
        "2 & 4 & 0\n",
        "\\end{array} \\right]\n",
        "\\sim\n",
        "\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc|c}\n",
        "1 & 2 & 0 \\\\\n",
        "0 & 0 & 0\n",
        "\\end{array} \\right].\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$x_2$ is free, $x_1=-2x_2.$ Let $x_2=-1$. Then $\\begin{bmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector for $\\lambda_1 = 0.$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\left[ A - 5I \\,\\middle|\\, \\mathbf{0} \\right] = \n",
        "\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc|c}\n",
        "-4 & 2 & 0 \\\\\n",
        "2 & -1 & 0\n",
        "\\end{array} \\right]\n",
        "\\sim\n",
        "\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc|c}\n",
        "1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\\n",
        "0 & 0 & 0\n",
        "\\end{array} \\right].\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Hence, $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix}$ is an eigenvector for $\\lambda_2$ = 5.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors{.really-really-smaller-title}\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{style=\"font-size: 1.35em\"}"
      ],
      "id": "60f0a541"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from IPython.core.display import HTML\n",
